  <layout>One page of text in a single column, with a vertical rule at the right; the scan shows only part of the printed page. Running head across the top. No margin notes.; One page of text in a single column, with a few short lines set as headings and indented sub-items; no marginal notes visible. The top line "IARUM." is the tail of a running or section heading cut off at the left edge.</layout>
  <running_head>MATER</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">Sui ipso jure sunt hæredes.</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Filius ab hostibus captus per fictionem</l>
    <l n="5">sui venit appellatione.</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Filius non succedit patri perduelli.</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Nepotes cum patruis admittuntur</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 7.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Quo tempore suus hæres esse dicatur?</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 8.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Nepos avo demum succedit, si eo vivo</l>
    <l n="14">fuerit conceptus.</l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 9.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Emancipatus nonnisi jure prætorio suc-</l>
    <l n="17">cedit.</l>
    <l n="18" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 10. 11. 12.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Quid statuendum de adoptivo?</l>
    <l n="20" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 13.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Jure prætorio juvatur adoptivus.</l>
    <l n="22" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 14.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Quid obtineat jure Justinianeo?</l>
    <l n="24" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 15. 16.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">1. Olim &amp; postmodum in sexu differentia</l>
    <l n="26">suit observata.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">2. Secus jure novissimo.</l>
    <l n="28" type="heading" level="1" para="true">LIBR. 3. INSTIT. TIT. 2.</l>
    <l n="29" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De legitimâ Agnatorum successione.</l>
    <l n="30" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="31" para="true">QUinam sint agnati?</l>
    <l n="32" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 1. 2.</l>
    <l n="33" para="true">Quinam agnatorum veniant nomine?</l>
    <l n="34" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="35" para="true">Quo sensu dicat Justinianus se 12.</l>
    <l n="36">tabulas esse secutum?</l>
    <l n="37" type="heading" level="1" para="true">IARUM.</l>
    <l n="38" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="39" para="true">Sexui favet Justinianus.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">§. 5. 6.</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">1. Graduum servatur differentia.</l>
    <l n="42" para="true">2. Quis dicatur proximior?</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">3. Etiam in casu quo relictus est usufru-</l>
    <l n="44">ctus conjugi cum onere restituendi bona</l>
    <l n="45">proximioribus.</l>
    <l n="46" para="true">§. 7.</l>
    <l n="47" para="true">Olim successorio edicto non erat locus.</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">§. 8.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">Pater succedit filio si eum contracta fiducia</l>
    <l n="50">emancipavit.</l>
    <l n="51" type="heading" level="1" caput="2" para="true">LIBR. 2. TIT. 3.</l>
    <l n="52" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Senatusconsulto Tertulliano.</l>
    <l n="53" para="true">In Princ. &amp; §. 1.</l>
    <l n="54" para="true">Praetor olim matrem ut cognatam ad</l>
    <l n="55">successionem admisit.</l>
    <l n="56" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="57" para="true">1. Per Tertullianum matri plenius consul-</l>
    <l n="58">tum.</l>
    <l n="59" para="true">2. Filia nupta remanet in potestate sui pa-</l>
    <l n="60">tris.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="62" para="true">Mater a quibusdam excluditur.</l>
    <l n="63" para="true">§. 4. 5.</l>
    <l n="64" para="true">Jus maternum incrementum sumpsit.</l>
    <l n="65" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="66" para="true">Sunt casus quibus mater liberorum suc-</l>
    <l n="67">cessione privatur.</l>
    <l n="68" type="heading" level="1" caput="3" para="true">LIBR. 3. INSTIT. TIT. 4.</l>
    <l n="69" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Sc. Orphitiano.</l>
    <l n="70" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="71" para="true">Liberi succedunt matri.</l>
    <l n="72" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="73" para="true">Non filii tantum, sed etiam nepotes suc-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The printed text is partly cut off at the bottom; the scan ends after the line on Quo sensu. Some words in the lower part of the page are faint, so the marginal-looking "Quinam" and the first initial "Q" of the last section are read with some doubt. The left edge of the scan is cut off, so the first letters of some lines are missing; the opening "IARUM." is likely the end of a word such as "PARUM" or "HARUM". Doubtful readings: "Praetor" is read from a partly cut initial letter. The page is cut off at the bottom right and the rest of the last line is missing.</notes>
</page>
